WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.870
Donald Trump's nightmare is now potentially
a reality.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:14.130
He is in a statistical tie with Joe Biden
in the red state of Texas in an election which

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.160
really could go either way in Texas.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.750
Now, I obviously don't have to tell you.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:25.120
If Joe Biden were to win Texas, this will
be a historic defeat for Donald Trump.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.430
This will be like something we've not seen
in a very long time in American politics.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:33.090
But I also shouldn't have to tell you by now,
but I will.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.610
That nothing is certain and everyone must
vote.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:40.300
So in one new poll from Texas, from The Dallas
Morning News, Joe Biden is now leading by

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.300
five.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.300
Forty eight to 43.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:48.200
Now, that's leaving nine percent in the third
party or undecided bucket.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.630
And they could break for the incumbent, Donald
Trump, between now and November.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.170
And they may well will.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.970
They may well do that.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:59.680
If you look at the averages of recent polling
in Texas, it's not as bad for Trump in the

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.780
real Clear Politics average.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.350
It's just a tie in the 538.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:08.070
Average, Trump is ahead by zero point one
percent.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:12.490
So understand that these are blended averages
looking at recent polls.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.500
I don't know.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.810
The exact numbers are so important, like if
it's a tie in Texas versus if Trump's winning

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:22.420
by zero point one or if Trump or Biden are
winning by one.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.280
The point is it's close in Texas and the story
is the trend line.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:32.710
Three, four months ago at the start of the
pandemic, five months ago now, Trump was solidly

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:36.000
ahead in every Texas poll by about five points.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.390
That lead has evaporated into what is.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.950
Now, listen, we can just say it's tight in
Texas.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:44.710
Now, if you say to me, David, you've got to
bet money who wins Texas in November?

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.140
I'm still betting Trump wins Texas.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:51.659
And in fact, if you look at the betting markets,
64 percent of people are still betting that

00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:57.360
Donald Trump wins the state of Texas, but
64 percent is actually quite low historically

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:04.369
because the last time that a Democratic presidential
candidate won in Texas was Jimmy Carter in

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:05.990
1976.

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:07.540
That's 44 years ago.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:14.859
So this could be a historic defeat for Donald
Trump or Trump might suppress just enough

00:02:14.859 --> 00:02:21.069
of the vote, lie and claim just enough of
an accomplishment, I guess, on corona virus

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:26.409
or the economy to convince just enough people
to vote for him.

00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:30.340
Just enough people might end up deciding to
stay home if vote by mail isn't happening

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.340
in their state.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:35.040
And they feel that it's dangerous to their
health to go out and vote and he could squeak

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.840
out another electoral win.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.800
Now, I want to be crystal clear about something
here.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:47.019
The nightmare of Trump getting crushed in
November will be nothing for him compared

00:02:47.019 --> 00:02:52.599
to the nightmare that he has subjected the
United States and the world to for the last

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:54.329
three and a half years.

00:02:54.329 --> 00:03:00.019
And Trump may not have the nightmare of losing
in November if we don't go vote and we get

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:03.829
voters registered and we make sure that everybody
votes.

00:03:03.829 --> 00:03:07.180
So this is the daily or weekly reminder.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.299
You've got to vote no matter what.

00:03:09.299 --> 00:03:13.159
Ask your friends if they are voting and encourage
them to do so.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:17.060
We do not want 2016 all over again.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.379
Now, Texas is interesting for another reason.

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:26.430
Texas is a story as much about gerrymandering
as it is about Donald Trump not doing well

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.309
when you look at the districts.

00:03:28.309 --> 00:03:29.309
Texas is red.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.340
There's no denying it.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:33.150
But Texas is much less red than many other
states.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.510
So, for example, Hillary Clinton got 43 percent
of the vote in 2016.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:40.049
In Texas, 43 percent of the vote.

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:45.829
For comparison, here in Massachusetts, Donald
Trump only got 32 percent of the vote.

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:47.909
So to put it a different way.

00:03:47.909 --> 00:03:54.559
Hillary Clinton's support in Texas was more
than a third larger than Trump's support here

00:03:54.559 --> 00:03:55.709
in Massachusetts.

00:03:55.709 --> 00:04:01.589
Texas is much more purple than many other
states that are considered solid red states.

00:04:01.589 --> 00:04:04.730
The thing about Texas is that it is hugely
gerrymandered.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:10.229
And when you look at the house reality in
the U.S. House of Representatives, when you

00:04:10.229 --> 00:04:16.160
look at the districts within Texas, at the
state level, the gerrymandering that has gone

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:21.600
on there is responsible for Texas seeming
much more red than it actually is, because

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:28.540
43 percent for the Democratic candidate in
a state that is considered to be one of the

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:29.740
reddest of red.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.310
Texas is increasingly purple.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.640
You look at places like Austin and other cities.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.960
It is a changing landscape.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:42.580
And let's see what we can do in 2020 to make
it maybe the start of the start of Texas being

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:43.600
a swing swing state.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.640
Texas being a battleground state, which would
be terrible at a systemic level for Republicans,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.760
as we've talked about many, many times.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.800
But assume nothing.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:56.430
Imagine that your one vote could be the deciding
vote in your state.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.440
If you knew that could be the case, you would
sure as hell go out and vote.

